en submitted (lines 451-459)\n6. Content is hidden on server side when not authenticated (line 210: {{if .Authenticated}})\n\n**What's missing (according to plan but not implemented):**\n1. Logout/clear key button in header that clears localStorage and shows modal\n\n**Issues with the plan:**\n1. The plan suggests creating /api/auth/validate endpoint - NOT NEEDED because validation already works via ?key= parameter\n2. The plan suggests blocking all content - but content IS blocked server-side via {{if .Authenticated}} conditional rendering, so this is already done\n3. The plan says \"add modal overlay HTML/CSS\" - already there\n4. The plan says \"add JavaScript to check localStorage\" - already there\n\nThe plan is largely describing existing functionality. The only real addition that would make sense is:\n- Adding a logout/clear key button\n\nHowever, looking at the original feature description again:\n\"The frontend should display a modal overlay prompting for the API key to allow access to the webui. The key is stored in localStorage for persistence. Without a valid key (either entered or stored), the backend should not send any actual data to the frontend - all content is blocked until authenticated.\"\n\nThis is ALREADY implemented! The modal exists, localStorage is used, and content is blocked server-side.\n\nWait - let me re-read the plan more carefully. \n\nThe plan's claim that \"all existing API endpoints continue to require auth (already implemented)\" needs verification. Looking at api.go, /api/clients requires checkAPIAuth() while /api/board uses checkDashboardAuth(). The plan doesn't clarify which key the modal should validate against, and since SERVER_DASHBOARD_KEY and SERVER_API_KEY are different environment variables, there's ambiguity about which one the frontend should be checking.","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":"850a550d8a883924f504b7ac7fb7e06772a18ee70dd38a81800cc03e9c3d596f"}]}}}}
